/**
 * @defgroup QuadGeo QuadGeo — Quadrupole Magnet Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the RHIC D0 dipole and Q1–Q3
 *        quadrupole focusing magnets (QUAD)
 *
 * @details
 * QuadGeo (module name QUADGEO) models the iron yokes of the final-focus
 * beam-line elements located in the east and west beam tunnels on either side
 * of the STAR interaction point.  These elements are the D0 dipole, Q1, Q2,
 * and Q3 quadrupole magnets of the RHIC beam optics.  Only the passive iron
 * yoke material is represented; the purpose is to account for material budget
 * effects on particles entering the ZDC and forward spectrometer regions.
 *
 * Four assemblies are placed symmetrically: east and west, each with two beam
 * lines offset ±26 cm in x and angled ±0.3° relative to the nominal z-axis,
 * reflecting the crossing geometry of the two RHIC rings at IR6.
 *
 * Each assembly is contained in a cylindrical air mother volume MGMT
 * (radius 19 cm, length 1610 cm) centred at z ≈ ±2485.26 cm.  Inside MGMT,
 * four iron tubes model the yokes:
 * - **DZER**: D0 dipole, rmin = 4.775 cm, rmax = 15.995 cm, L = 385.26 cm.
 * - **QONE**: Q1 quadrupole, rmin = ri1 = 6.355 cm, rmax = 18.28 cm, L = 170.92 cm.
 * - **QTWO**: Q2 quadrupole, rmin = 6.355 cm, rmax = 18.28 cm, L = 444.02 cm.
 * - **QTHR**: Q3 quadrupole, rmin = 6.355 cm, rmax = 18.28 cm, L = 399.55 cm.
 *
 * There is a single geometry configuration (SHLQ version 1).  The module is
 * enabled via the QUADon setup and disabled via QUADof.
 *
 * ## Setup configurations
 *
 * | Setup name | onoff | Description |
 * |------------|-------|-------------|
 * | QUADof     | off   | Quadrupole magnets disabled |
 * | QUADon     | on    | Default quadrupole configuration |
 *
 * ## Volume hierarchy
 * @code
 * MGMT  (TUBE Air — mother, placed ×4 in CAVE at ±x, ±z, ±angle)
 * ├── DZER  (TUBE Iron — D0 dipole yoke)
 * ├── QONE  (TUBE Iron — Q1 quadrupole yoke)
 * ├── QTWO  (TUBE Iron — Q2 quadrupole yoke)
 * └── QTHR  (TUBE Iron — Q3 quadrupole yoke)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file QuadGeo.xml
 * @brief RHIC D0 + Q1–Q3 quadrupole magnet geometry (QUADGEO module).
 * Four assemblies at ±z ≈ 2485 cm, ±x = 26 cm, ±0.3° crossing angle.
 * SHLQ version 1 geometry parameters.
 * Author: Maxim Potekhin (2 September 2005).
 */

